{%- doc -%}
  Motion 14.2.0 (https://motion.dev, MIT): self-hosted UMD build from the
  official `motion` npm package (dist/motion.js), saved as assets/motion.min.js.

  layout/theme.liquid renders this in <head> after the GSAP bundle, only on
  pages where template markup contains `data-motion-dev` (and always in the
  theme editor), so it costs nothing elsewhere. `defer`, like GSAP: it runs
  before any deferred script later in the document.

  Use the `Motion` global from a deferred or module script:
    const { animate, scroll, inView, stagger, spring } = window.Motion;
    animate('.cv-thing', { opacity: [0, 1], y: [16, 0] }, { duration: 0.6 });
  Respect reduced motion as the GSAP sections do.

  assets/cv-motion-dev.js follows it: the theme's own Motion modules
  (data-motion-dev="cards" product grids, data-motion-dev="faq" accordions).

  Full official license: assets/motion-LICENSE.txt.
  To upgrade: replace assets/motion.min.js with dist/motion.js from a verified
  pinned `motion` release, keep its license, and update the version here.

  @example
  {% render 'motion' %}
{%- enddoc -%}
<script src="{{ 'motion.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'cv-motion-dev.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
